OL,3,GNEWSA'Illustrating Brideshead Revisited
OL,4,Awas a privilege'
OL,5,
OL,6,F"People told me they wanted to read the
OL,7,Fbook after seeing my illustrations."
OL,9,FIt took Oxford-based artist Weimin He
OL,10,Fnearly a year to create his "deeply
OL,11,Fimmersive", yet "challenging" project -
OL,12,Fthe first illustrations for a Chinese
OL,13,Fedition of Evelyn Waugh's Brideshead
OL,14,FRevisited, published in August.
OL,16,FHaving lived in the city for more than
OL,17,F20 years, he said it was "a privilege"
OL,18,Fto have depicted local places featured
OL,19,Fin the novel and to have researched
OL,20,Fwhat they were like in the 1920s and
OL,21,F1930s.
OL,23,APub: 13-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
